# Local artifact mirror (dev only — prod writes to R2). Layered so the
# per-customer exceptions below actually work: a whole-dir ignore
# (`local-artifacts/`) is final in git — negations under it are dead letters,
# which is why the old exceptions only "worked" for force-added files.
local-artifacts/*
!local-artifacts/customers/
local-artifacts/customers/*
# Exception: the `demo` customer seed is checked in so a fresh clone has
# working fixture data for the Magic Moment sprint and integration tests.
!local-artifacts/customers/demo/
# Exception: the `streamly_sample` customer — second-vertical sample fixture
# (streaming) used to pressure-test that the simulator isn't food-delivery-shaped.
!local-artifacts/customers/streamly_sample/
# Exception: the `streamly-sandbox` customer — the first crawler-GENERATED pack
# (sidira-crawler synthesize-pack run, 2026-W24), imported verbatim from R2 in
# #190. GENERATED, NEVER AUTHORED: never hand-edit these files; re-import from
# R2 instead.
!local-artifacts/customers/streamly-sandbox/
# Runtime output written into allowlisted customers (simulation runs from the
# test suite / local dev) stays out of git regardless of the allowlist above.
local-artifacts/customers/*/simulations/
